                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Araya is a game made by a rather exotic studio from Malaysia, which caught my attention. I expected something original in terms of the story and was ready to overlook the shortcomings typical of games made by small independent developers.\n\nUnfortunately, the game was rather disappointing. What we get is a typical \"walking simulator\", offering virtually no interaction apart from collecting a few items that have to be used somewhere else. The story isn't anything special either — we get, as in pretty much every Asian horror, the ghost of a young girl who died and is now seeking revenge.\n\nThe game takes place over a single night in an abandoned hospital, which is visited by several people for different reasons, and their stories are intertwined in a way. But everything is presented so enigmatically (another common problem with many similar games) that I had to look up the Wikipedia entry just to make some sense of it all.\n\nI did make it to the end — although I was driven more by the desire to finish the game than by any actual interest in it. Fortunately, the game isn't long, runs relatively well without any major bugs, and its aesthetics are very loosely reminiscent of the fantastic Silent Hill series. So, if you're really looking for something to kill some time with, you could give it a try.",
